33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,I saw the station block’s bin house. It’s a trap. The smell is worse because it’s sealed in. We can’t just copy them.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,I checked the ledger. We spend thirty-four thousand yen a year on deodorant and call-outs. That’s a lot for five houses.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I read the complaint log. Eleven out of fourteen complaints came from the house next to the gate. That’s not a bin problem, that’s a boundary problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"I timed the truck. It’s here at seven forty. If I have to be up at seven to clear the pavement, I’m losing an hour of sleep. That’s not a hobby.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"I measured the frontages. Two houses have wide bays, one is crossed by a driveway, and the narrowest leaves ninety centimetres of pavement. The current site sits on the narrowest frontage.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Midori, thirty-four thousand yen is a lot, but is it more than the cost of my sanity? I need to know if a different layout changes the smell.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, the ledger shows the money goes to fixing the mess, not preventing it. If we stop the mess, the money stops. That’s the point.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, ninety centimetres is the problem. The current site is on the narrowest frontage, and the complaints come from the house next to the gate. We are asking the most squeezed house to host the most traffic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, that’s the labor trap. If the narrowest house hosts the traffic, they become the de facto manager. I don’t want to be that person. I need a system that doesn’t rely on one person’s goodwill.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, I agree. The measurements show the current site is on the narrowest frontage. The filing requirements say a permanent build needs five signatures and four months. We can’t just move it without a formal process.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I’m leaning toward the supervised mornings. If we all take turns, no one is the manager. But I need to know if the smell is still there.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,I’m leaning toward the low-cost option. The ledger shows we can save thirty-four thousand yen a year if we stop the mess. I don’t want to spend more to fix a problem we created.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I’m leaning toward the option that moves the site to the widest frontage. It’s not about the money, it’s about the boundary. If the widest house hosts the traffic, the narrowest house gets its peace.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"I’m leaning toward the option that has a clear, written schedule. I don’t want to be the one answering the phone. I want a system that runs itself.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I’m leaning toward the option that moves the site to the widest frontage. The measurements show it’s the only fair option. The filing requirements say we need five signatures, so we have to agree on it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I hope the supervised mornings work. I don’t want to smell garbage at 7 AM, but I don’t want to be the one who has to clean it up either.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I hope the low-cost option works. I don’t want to start a fight over a few hundred yen, but I don’t want to pay for a problem we created.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I hope the move to the widest frontage works. I don’t want to become strangers on this lane, but I don’t want to be the one who has to host the traffic.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I hope the written schedule works. I don’t want to be the one answering the phone, but I don’t want to be the one who has to clean it up either.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I hope the move to the widest frontage works. I don’t want to sign a document that is technically legal but morally bankrupt, but I don’t want to be the one who has to host the traffic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
